      "title": "Multiplying a 3x3 Matrix by a Column Vector"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Compute the following:\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{aligned}-3\\cdot 1 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\cdot (0) & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,(-2)\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot 1 & + & (-3)\\cdot (0) & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,1\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-4)\\cdot 1 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3\\cdot (0) & + & (-3)\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & + & (0) & + & (-4) \\\\ (-3) & + & 0 & + & 2 \\\\ (-4) & + & (0) & + & (-6)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
